// array_remove_unordered of a resizable array whose count says it has
// elements but whose data is null (issue #158, spec 3.17, 8.4): that count
// claims elements no memory holds, so the built-in stops as indexing such
// a view would, at its name, rather than moving its last element through
// null.
main :: () {
    a : [..]int;
    a.count = 2;
    array_remove_unordered(*a, 0);
}
